\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces (a) Occupations of the different sites, showing how close they are to being empty or fully occupied (y-log scale). In blue: diagonal elements of the correlation matrix. In orange: eigenvalues of the bath density matrix $\rho _\text  {bath}$. The threshold $\epsilon =10^{-6}$ is also indicated as an example. (b) New Hamiltonian after the first rotation $P$, defined by the eigenvectors of $\rho _\text  {bath}$, applied to the star representation of the AIM. The first site corresponds to the impurity, while the sixth site corresponds to the active site.\relax }}{6}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:first_rotation}{{4}{6}{(a) Occupations of the different sites, showing how close they are to being empty or fully occupied (y-log scale). In blue: diagonal elements of the correlation matrix. In orange: eigenvalues of the bath density matrix $\rho _\bath $. The threshold $\epsilon =10^{-6}$ is also indicated as an example. (b) New Hamiltonian after the first rotation $P$, defined by the eigenvectors of $\rho _\bath $, applied to the star representation of the AIM. The first site corresponds to the impurity, while the sixth site corresponds to the active site.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
